      "originalText": "- Pause tracking per team",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JJj9F7Sy7L3Dj70PL-nrg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4966.305822441975,
      "y": 2473.1931395995,
      "width": 412.40102641096223,
      "height": 100.09747535899359,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 426287967,
      "version": 1024,
      "versionNonce": 1265728959,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1775079321174,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "match_session — live draft state that's ephemeral and changes every turn:\n  - turnIndex, draftSequence (the full draft script)\n  - timerState (turn clock, reserves, pause state)\n  - Auction state (nomination, bids, budgets per team)\n  - Pause tracking per team\n\nWhy separate from lobby: lobby is the room config (settings, who's in it). Match session is the live\n  game state (whose turn, what's been drafted). They have different lifecycles — a lobby exists before\n  and after a match, but match_session only exists during active play and gets cleaned up after\n  finalization. Keeping draft state in lobby would bloat the lobby row with columns that are irrelevant\n   90% of the time (pre-match, post-match).",
      "fontSize": 7.279816389744984,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "match_session — live draft state that's ephemeral and changes every turn:\n  - turnIndex, draftSequence (the full draft script)\n  - timerState (turn clock, reserves, pause state)\n  - Auction state (nomination, bids, budgets per team)\n  - Pause tracking per team\n\nWhy separate from lobby: lobby is the room config (settings, who's in it). Match session is the live\n  game state (whose turn, what's been drafted). They have different lifecycles — a lobby exists before\n  and after a match, but match_session only exists during active play and gets cleaned up after\n  finalization. Keeping draft state in lobby would bloat the lobby row with columns that are irrelevant\n   90% of the time (pre-match, post-match).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NQYOKvyCaG-G3noQkSKmG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4967.864171521561,
      "y": 2419.6354525572515,
      "width": 350.7319291453765,
      "height": 28.468540232815037,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bE1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 701969279,
      "version": 753,
      "versionNonce": 1494838751,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1775079321174,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "match_session_step — the action log (event sourcing):\n  - Each row = one player action (pick, ban, bid)\n  - sequence for strict ordering, actorUserId, actorSlot, action, payload, timestamp",
      "fontSize": 7.591610728750676,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "match_session_step — the action log (event sourcing):\n  - Each row = one player action (pick, ban, bid)\n  - sequence for strict ordering, actorUserId, actorSlot, action, payload, timestamp",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
